  "notes": "Entrance is based on an evaluative audition, not modeled directly. New voice_catalog.json (VOICE 110/412/462); greatly extended thea_catalog.json and dance_catalog.json with the Musical Theatre Theory (THEA 113/116/212/214) and Performance (THEA 223/224/423/424) sequences, DANCE's ballet/jazz/tap technique ladder (231/232/241/242/251/252), and the musical-theatre-specific DANCE 382/384. Real gap fixed: DANCE 232 requires DANCE 230 (Ballet) as a real prereq, but the bulletin's own Suggested Academic Plan never otherwise schedules it -- added as an explicit Semester 1 item. Real gap fixed: THEA 425A requires THEA 425C as an enforced concurrent, but the Musical Theatre plan (unlike Acting B.F.A., which already schedules both) never otherwise schedules THEA 425C -- added as an explicit Semester 3 item. DANCE 251 could not be independently confirmed (its own description page didn't surface after six search attempts) despite being a real, active code (cited verbatim as DANCE 252's prereq) -- title/credits inferred from the DANCE 231/241/251 'Beginning X I' naming pattern rather than left unmodeled or guessed at from nothing. The bulletin's own 'Advanced Dance Elective' and 'Chorale Ensemble' items DO name real enumerated pools elsewhere on the program page (unlike Art B.A.'s unresolvable concentrations) -- modeled with one literal pick each (DANCE 431 for the dance elective, THEA 428 for the chorale ensemble, chosen since its 2cr matches that item's credits exactly) rather than the full pool, since each item is used only once. VOICE 110 (max 16cr, offered every semester) is scheduled 4 times -- one literal pick, three generic repeat slots, same convention as WFED 395/ARCH 491. THEA 113's own catalog page states 2cr while the program's Suggested Academic Plan table states 3cr for the same slot -- modeled at 3cr to match the plan's own semester total, documented as a real bulletin-internal discrepancy. This plan's computed credit total (~127.5cr) runs slightly over the bulletin's stated 125cr program total, a similar minor reconciliation gap to other majors built this session.",
